select 'mwfkbieber29', '{"texts": ["Canadian-born singer Justin Bieber has received Korean citizenship. The reason is very simple: he loves kimchi. In his citizenship test, he named twenty kinds of kimchi.", "These days Bieber eats kimchi three times a day: kimchi fried rice for breakfast, kimchi stew for lunch and a kimchi pancake for dinner. Even his snack is kkakdugi, and he takes a kimchi refrigerator along to his concerts abroad.", "Bieber also studied Korean hard. The very first word he learned was ''ppalli-ppalli'' (hurry, hurry). Now he always presses the elevator''s door-close button twice, and he greets friends with ''Have you eaten?''", "\"I can''t live without kimchi,\" Bieber told reporters. Then he added with a laugh, \"The title of my next album is ''Kkakdugi.''\"", "There are now five big kimchi jars in the yard of his house, and his neighbors call him ''the Kimchi Prince.'' Next month he will also make kimjang, and he has already bought a whopping 100 heads of napa cabbage."], "sentences": [{"text": "캐나다 출신 가수 저스틴 비버가 한국 국적을 받았어요.", "translation": "Canadian-born singer Justin Bieber has received Korean citizenship.", "vocab": [{"ko": "출신", "en": "origin; from (a place)"}, {"ko": "가수", "en": "singer"}, {"ko": "국적", "en": "nationality; citizenship"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to get"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "N 출신", "exp": "''From / born in N'': 캐나다 출신 가수 ''a singer from Canada''.", "example_in_sentence": "캐나다 출신"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject)", "exp": "Subject particle: 저스틴 비버 + 가. 가 follows a vowel, 이 a consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "비버가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Polite past ending: 받다 → 받았어요 ''received''. The stem 받 has ㅏ, so it takes 았어요.", "example_in_sentence": "받았어요"}]}, {"text": "이유는 아주 간단해요.", "translation": "The reason is very simple.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이유", "en": "reason"}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very"}, {"ko": "간단하다", "en": "to be simple"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic)", "exp": "Topic particle: 이유 + 는 ''as for the reason''. 는 follows a vowel, 은 a consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "이유는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Polite present ending. 하다 words become 해요: 간단하다 → 간단해요 ''is simple''.", "example_in_sentence": "간단해요"}]}, {"text": "김치를 너무 좋아하기 때문이에요.", "translation": "It is because he loves kimchi so much.", "vocab": [{"ko": "김치", "en": "kimchi"}, {"ko": "너무", "en": "so (much); really"}, {"ko": "좋아하다", "en": "to like; to love"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object)", "exp": "Object particle: 김치 + 를 shows what he loves. 를 follows a vowel, 을 a consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "김치를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "''It is because …'': 좋아하다 → 좋아하기 때문이에요 ''it is because (he) loves''.", "example_in_sentence": "좋아하기 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "비버는 국적 시험에서 김치 이름을 스무 개 말했어요.", "translation": "In his citizenship test, Bieber named twenty kinds of kimchi.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시험", "en": "test; exam"}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name"}, {"ko": "스무", "en": "twenty (before a counter)"}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say; to name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (place of action)", "exp": "Marks where something happens: 시험 + 에서 ''in the test''.", "example_in_sentence": "시험에서"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "number + 개", "exp": "개 counts things: 스무 개 ''twenty (of them)''. 스물 ''twenty'' becomes 스무 before a counter.", "example_in_sentence": "스무 개"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Polite past. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 말하다 → 말했어요 ''said; named''.", "example_in_sentence": "말했어요"}]}, {"text": "비버는 요즘 하루에 세 번 김치를 먹어요.", "translation": "These days, Bieber eats kimchi three times a day.", "vocab": [{"ko": "요즘", "en": "these days"}, {"ko": "하루", "en": "a day"}, {"ko": "번", "en": "time(s)"}, {"ko": "먹다", "en": "to eat"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "N에 (per)", "exp": "에 after a unit of time can mean ''per'': 하루에 ''a day; per day''.", "example_in_sentence": "하루에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "number + 번", "exp": "번 counts times: 세 번 ''three times''. 셋 ''three'' becomes 세 before a counter.", "example_in_sentence": "세 번"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Polite present ending: 먹다 → 먹어요 ''eats''. The stem 먹 has ㅓ, so it takes 어요.", "example_in_sentence": "먹어요"}]}, {"text": "아침에는 김치볶음밥, 점심에는 김치찌개, 저녁에는 김치전을 먹어요.", "translation": "He has kimchi fried rice for breakfast, kimchi stew for lunch and a kimchi pancake for dinner.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아침", "en": "morning; breakfast"}, {"ko": "김치볶음밥", "en": "kimchi fried rice"}, {"ko": "김치찌개", "en": "kimchi stew"}, {"ko": "김치전", "en": "kimchi pancake"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "에는 (time + topic)", "exp": "에 ''at (a time)'' + 는 (topic) sets times side by side: 아침에는 … 점심에는 … 저녁에는 … ''for breakfast … for lunch … for dinner …''.", "example_in_sentence": "아침에는"}]}, {"text": "간식도 깍두기예요.", "translation": "Even his snack is kkakdugi.", "vocab": [{"ko": "간식", "en": "snack"}, {"ko": "깍두기", "en": "kkakdugi (cubed radish kimchi)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "N도", "exp": "''Also; even'': 간식 + 도 ''his snack, too / even his snack''.", "example_in_sentence": "간식도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요/예요", "exp": "''Is / are'': 깍두기 ends in a vowel, so it takes 예요. After a consonant, use 이에요.", "example_in_sentence": "깍두기예요"}]}, {"text": "외국 공연에도 김치 냉장고를 가지고 가요.", "translation": "He even takes a kimchi refrigerator along to his concerts abroad.", "vocab": [{"ko": "외국", "en": "foreign country; abroad"}, {"ko": "공연", "en": "concert; performance"}, {"ko": "김치 냉장고", "en": "kimchi refrigerator"}, {"ko": "가지고 가다", "en": "to take (along)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "에도 (에 + 도)", "exp": "에 ''to'' + 도 ''even; also'': 공연에도 ''even to (his) concerts''.", "example_in_sentence": "공연에도"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "가지고 가다", "exp": "''To take (something) along'': 가지다 ''to have'' + 고 + 가다 ''to go''.", "example_in_sentence": "가지고 가요"}]}, {"text": "비버는 한국어도 열심히 공부했어요.", "translation": "Bieber also studied Korean hard.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한국어", "en": "Korean (language)"}, {"ko": "열심히", "en": "hard; diligently"}, {"ko": "공부하다", "en": "to study"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "N도", "exp": "''Also'': 한국어 + 도 ''Korean, too''.", "example_in_sentence": "한국어도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Polite past. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 공부하다 → 공부했어요 ''studied''.", "example_in_sentence": "공부했어요"}]}, {"text": "제일 먼저 배운 말은 ''빨리빨리''예요.", "translation": "The very first word he learned was ''ppalli-ppalli'' (hurry, hurry).", "vocab": [{"ko": "제일 먼저", "en": "first of all; the very first"}, {"ko": "배우다", "en": "to learn"}, {"ko": "말", "en": "word; words"}, {"ko": "빨리빨리", "en": "quickly, quickly; hurry, hurry"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs: 배우다 → 배운 말 ''the word (he) learned''.", "example_in_sentence": "배운 말"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "제일 먼저", "exp": "''First of all; the very first'': 제일 ''most'' + 먼저 ''first''.", "example_in_sentence": "제일 먼저"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요/예요", "exp": "After a word that ends in a vowel, 예요 means ''is'': ''빨리빨리''예요.", "example_in_sentence": "''빨리빨리''예요"}]}, {"text": "요즘은 엘리베이터를 타면 닫힘 버튼을 꼭 두 번 눌러요.", "translation": "These days, whenever he gets in an elevator, he always presses the door-close button twice.", "vocab": [{"ko": "엘리베이터", "en": "elevator"}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to get on; to ride"}, {"ko": "닫힘 버튼", "en": "door-close button"}, {"ko": "누르다", "en": "to press"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "''If / when(ever)'': 타다 → 타면 ''when he gets on''. After a vowel, just add 면.", "example_in_sentence": "타면"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "꼭", "exp": "''Always; without fail'': 꼭 두 번 눌러요 ''always presses (it) twice''.", "example_in_sentence": "꼭 두 번"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "르 irregular", "exp": "Verbs ending in 르 add an extra ㄹ befo