th, Bieber is also going to do kimjang, making a big batch of kimchi for the winter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다음 달", "en": "next month"}, {"ko": "김장", "en": "kimjang (making a big batch of kimchi for the winter)"}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "N에 (time)", "exp": "에 after a time word means ''in / at'': 다음 달에 ''next month''.", "example_in_sentence": "다음 달에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "N도", "exp": "''Also'': 김장 + 도 ''kimjang, too''.", "example_in_sentence": "김장도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요", "exp": "Future: 하다 → 할 거예요 ''will do''.", "example_in_sentence": "할 거예요"}]}, {"text": "배추를 벌써 100포기나 샀어요.", "translation": "He has already bought a whopping 100 heads of napa cabbage.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배추", "en": "napa cabbage"}, {"ko": "벌써", "en": "already"}, {"ko": "포기", "en": "head (counter for cabbages)"}, {"ko": "사다", "en": "to buy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "number + (이)나 (as many as)", "exp": "나 after a number means ''as many as'': the speaker thinks it is a lot. 100포기나 ''a whole 100 heads''. After a consonant, use 이나.", "example_in_sentence": "100포기나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Polite past: 사다 → 샀어요 ''bought'' (사 + 았 → 샀).", "example_in_sentence": "샀어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', '[{"ko": "출신", "en": "origin; from (a place)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가수", "en": "singer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국적", "en": "nationality; citizenship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to get", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very", "note": ""}, {"ko": "간단하다", "en": "to be simple", "note": ""}, {"ko": "김치", "en": "kimchi", "note": ""}, {"ko": "너무", "en": "so (much); really", "note": ""}, {"ko": "좋아하다", "en": "to like; to love", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시험", "en": "test; exam", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "스무", "en": "twenty (before a counter)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say; to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "요즘", "e