en": "five", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이웃", "en": "neighbor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "왕자", "en": "prince", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다음 달", "en": "next month", "note": ""}, {"ko": "김장", "en": "kimjang (making a big batch of kimchi for the winter)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배추", "en": "napa cabbage", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벌써", "en": "already", "note": ""}, {"ko": "포기", "en": "head (counter for cabbages)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사다", "en": "to buy", "note": ""}]', '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite past ending: 받다 → 받았어요 ''received''. The stem 받 has ㅏ, so it takes 았어요.", "ex_ko": "캐나다 출신 가수 저스틴 비버가 한국 국적을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "Canadian-born singer Justin Bieber has received Korean citizenship."}, {"name": "~기 때문이다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''It is because …'': 좋아하다 → 좋아하기 때문이에요 ''it is because (he) loves''.", "ex_ko": "김치를 너무 좋아하기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It is because he loves kimchi so much."}, {"name": "~에서 (place of action)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks where something happens: 시험 + 에서 ''in the test''.", "ex_ko": "비버는 국적 시험에서 김치 이름을 스무 개 말했어요.", "ex_en": "In his citizenship test, Bieber named twenty kinds of kimchi."}, {"name": "N에 (per)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "에 after a unit of time can mean ''per'': 하루에 ''a day; per day''.", "ex_ko": "비버는 요즘 하루에 세 번 김치를 먹어요.", "ex_en": "These days, Bieber eats kimchi three times a day."}, {"name": "에는 (time + topic)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "에 ''at (a time)'' + 는 (topic) sets times side by side: 아침에는 … 점심에는 … 저녁에는 … ''for breakfast … for lunch … for dinner …''.", "ex_ko": "아침에는 김치볶음밥, 점심에는 김치찌개, 저녁에는 김치전을 먹어요.", "ex_en": "He has kimchi fried rice for breakfast, kimchi stew for lunch and a kimchi pancake for dinner."}, {"name": "N도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Also; even'': 간식 + 도 ''his snack, too / even his snack''.", "ex_ko": "간식도 깍두기예요.", "ex_en": "Even his snack is kkakdugi."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs: 배우다 → 배운 말 ''the word (he) learned''.", "ex_ko": "제일 먼저 배운 말은 ''빨리빨리''예요.", "ex_en": "The very first word he learned was ''ppalli-ppalli'' (hurry, hurry)."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''If / when(ever)'': 타다 → 타면 ''when he gets on''. After a vowel, just add 면.", "ex_ko": "요즘은 엘리베이터를 타면 닫힘 버튼을 꼭 두 번 눌러요.", "ex_en": "These days, whenever he gets in an elevator, he always presses the door-close button twice."}, {"name": "르 irregular", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Verbs ending in 르 add an extra ㄹ before 아/어: 누르다 → 눌러요 ''presses''.", "ex_ko": "요즘은 엘리베이터를 타면 닫힘 버튼을 꼭 두 번 눌러요.", "ex_en": "These days, whenever he gets in an elevator, he always presses the door-close button twice."}, {"name": "~라고 (direct quote)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Put after a quote: the quoted words + 라고 + a verb of saying (말하다, 인사하다 …). ''밥 먹었어요?''라고 인사해요 ''greets (them) by saying \"Have you eaten?\"''.", "ex_ko": "친구를 만나면 ''밥 먹었어요?''라고 인사해요.", "ex_en": "When he meets friends, he greets them with ''Have you eaten?''"}, {"name": "~에게 (to someone)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''To (a person)'': 기자들 + 에게 ''to the reporters''.", "ex_ko": "비버는 기자들에게 \"김치 없으면 못 살아요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "Bieber told reporters, \"I can''t live without kimchi.\""}, {"name": "못 + verb", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Cannot'': 못 before a verb: 못 살아요 ''can''t live''.", "ex_ko": "비버는 기자들에게 \"김치 없으면 못 살아요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "Bieber told reporters, \"I can''t live without kimchi.\""}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''While …ing'': 웃다 → 웃으면서 말했어요 ''said while laughing''. After a consonant, add 으면서.", "ex_ko": "그리고 \"다음 앨범 제목은 ''깍두기''예요\"라고 웃으면서 말했어요.", "ex_en": "Then he said with a laugh, \"The title of my next album is ''Kkakdugi.''\""}, {"name": "N을/를 N(이)라고 부르다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''To call N (something)'': 비버를 ''김치 왕자''라고 불러요 ''call Bieber \"the Kimchi Prince\"''.", "ex_ko": "이웃들은 비버를 ''김치 왕자''라고 불러요.", "ex_en": "His neighbors call Bieber ''the Kimchi Prince.''"}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Future: 하다 → 할 거예요 ''will do''.", "ex_ko": "비버는 다음 달에 김장도 할 거예요.", "ex_en": "Next month, Bieber is also going to do kimjang, making a big batch of kimchi for the winter."}]}', '{"questions":[{"sentence":"비버는 요즘 하루에 _____ 번 김치를 먹어요.","sentence_en":"These days, Bieber eats kimchi _____ times a day.","blank":"세","blank_en":"three","choices":["세","한","열","백"]},{"sentence":"간식도 _____예요.","sentence_en":"Even his snack is _____.","blank":"깍두기","blank_en":"kkakdugi","choices":["깍두기","초콜릿","사탕","과자"]},{"sentence":"외국 공연에도 김치 _____를 가지고 가요.","sentence_en":"He even takes a kimchi _____ along to his concerts abroad.","blank":"냉장고","blank_en":"refrigerator","choices":["냉장고","세탁기","자동차","컴퓨터"]},{"sentence":"제일 먼저 배운 말은 ''_____''예요.","sentence_en":"The very first word he learned was ''_____''.","blank":"빨리빨리","blank_en":"ppalli-ppalli (hurry, hurry)","choices":["빨리빨리","천천히","조용히","안녕히"]},{"sentence":"요즘은 엘리베이터를 타면 닫힘 버튼을 꼭 두 번 _____.","sentence_en":"These days, whenever he gets in an elevator, he always _____ the door-close button twice.","blank":"눌러요","blank_en":"presses","choices":["눌러요","그려요","씻어요","먹어요"]}]}', '[{"phrase":"김치 없으면 못 살아요","note":"I can''t live without kimchi","color":"amber"},{"phrase":"밥 먹었어요?","note":"Have you eaten? (a friendly greeting)","color":"amber"},{"phrase":"제일 먼저","note":"first of all; the very first","color":"amber"}]', now()
 where not exists (select 1 from public.article_cache where article_id = 'mwfkbieber29');
